<title>BELGIUM: EU may publish rule ending wheat export tax.</title>
<headline>EU may publish rule ending wheat export tax.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A European Union regulation abolishing soft wheat export taxes at weekly grain tenders may be published in the EU Official Journal on Friday, a European Commission official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The official said the Commission still has to approve the regulation under the so-called written procedure which expires at noon on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;The earliest it could be published is Friday,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The EU's cereals management committee unanimously voted last Thursday to end the tax tenders for soft wheat, following a fall in world prices.</p>
<p>The tax was introduced last December in a move to ensure adequate supplies for domestic consumers at affordable prices after world prices soared above EU levels.</p>
</text>
